# Usage stats

Settings section `usage-stats` is the desktop restyle of `dsh-usage-panel`. Tokens / `ui-primitives` only; billing = ESTIMATE (peak/valley buckets × user prices, official price table asOf 2026-08-17 with source link); no `/user/balance`, no balance APIs. Unpriced models show "set a price"/em dash, never a guessed figure (competitor red line stands). Peak/valley windows: Beijing UTC+8 Monday–Friday 09:00–12:00 & 14:00–18:00; a step bills at its step/start instant; compaction never enters cost buckets. UTC day buckets in v1. Desktop `desktop-plugins` copy wins over a marketplace install of the same package. Empty state is no billed usage (blank-only sessions included) with no scan failures; light heatmap empty cells must stay visible. Mounting rides the desktop overlay `desktop-usage-panel.patch.yml` (`--patch`, full starts only) — never a managed block in the user-owned `cordis.patch.yml`; the overlay is deleted when disabled, ensure fails, or a marketplace bundle already mounts the package. The plugin client registers ONLY `settings.section` — never a `conversation.composer.dock` entry: the peak/valley status + session-cost row under the composer belongs to the harness `PeakValleyRow` (session-cost-display card), and a plugin-side strip duplicated that line after the pr-76/pr-79 merge (removed 2026-09-02). **Prices have one editor and one record**: the editor is this page's 计费设置 modal (the harness price panel and both of its buttons are gone as of 2026-09-13) and the record is `ui-conversation.sessionCostPrices`, which the plugin host reads AND writes through the settings service so the composer strip reprices on save; the plugin's own `dsh_usage_panel_billing` domain is import-only and its record is merged into the conversation section once (section wins). The modal no longer renders the official price table. Session cost prices every billed model route at its own column, so a multi-model conversation totals correctly.

